[00:00.00]ESLPod.com and the Center for Educational Development present to you introduction to
[00:20.42]the United States, a 100 episode course that will teach you about life in the United States,
[00:29.54]including its government and history. This course is based upon the 100 questions used by the
[00:41.38]US government in its citizenship examination and includes basic information about the US and its
[00:53.54]people. Each episode of the course begins with a basic question about the US followed by a short
[01:05.62]answer and then a detailed explanation of that answer. Each episode is first presented at a slow
[01:18.26]speed and then at a normal rate of speech. All of the episodes include a special learning guide
[01:30.66]that contains the complete transcript of the episode as well as vocabulary definitions and sample
[01:41.38]sentences using the new terms. We hope you enjoy this special course. This course has been a
[01:52.74]production of the Center for Educational Development in beautiful Los Angeles, California.
